  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342125",
      "title": "Working with Union Types",
      "lectureOrder": 500,
      "videoOrder": 442,
      "sourceHash": "edf42df1fd61444c579b3ac6f37df243b331dbc576db9c6eeaa4f1f1be55f63c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.35,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "So now we added the configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 5.73,
          "en": "Now let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 10.73,
          "en": "we actually want to make add a bit more flexible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.78,
          "end": 12.26,
          "en": "It should work with numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.26,
          "end": 14.75,
          "en": "but it should also work with strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.75,
          "end": 18.07,
          "en": "Of course I wanted to ensure that it works with numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.07,
          "end": 21.08,
          "en": "to show you why TypeScript is awesome,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.08,
          "end": 23.08,
          "en": "but still, this could be a use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.08,
          "end": 25.13,
          "en": "that you have in some app you are building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.13,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "You want to allow both numbers and strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 33.2,
          "en": "because maybe here, we want to have a string result as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.26,
          "end": 35.65,
          "en": "And there, I want to be able to call add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.65,
          "end": 37.42,
          "en": "with the string values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.42,
          "end": 40.89,
          "en": "And I want to get that concatenated result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.89,
          "end": 45.89,
          "en": "So I want to have that concatenated string of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 48.82,
          "en": "Now, currently we are only accepting number here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.82,
          "end": 50.7,
          "en": "We could change this to any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.7,
          "end": 53.23,
          "en": "Now any kind of data is accepted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.23,
          "end": 56.35,
          "en": "But as a downside, we can now, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.35,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "also console.log add, and add true and false together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.91,
          "end": 64.69,
          "en": "Now I don't want to accept Booleans,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.69,
          "end": 67.31,
          "en": "I want to accept strings and numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.31,
          "end": 70.733,
          "en": "That's where we can use a feature called the Union Type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.72,
          "end": 74.25,
          "en": "Often in code, you will have code that works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.25,
          "end": 76.13,
          "en": "with more than one type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.13,
          "end": 76.97,
          "en": "Now in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.97,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "you can define multiple types, like number and string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 84.6,
          "en": "separated with that single pipe symbol here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.6,
          "end": 85.84,
          "en": "This is a Union Type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.84,
          "end": 89.74,
          "en": "It means number num1 is either a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.74,
          "end": 90.90299999999999,
          "en": "or a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 95.37,
          "en": "And we can do this here for num2 as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.37,
          "end": 98.25,
          "en": "Now we get an error here because of that Union Type thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.25,
          "end": 101.27000000000001,
          "en": "because even though the plus operator does work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.27000000000001,
          "end": 103.15,
          "en": "with both number and string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.15,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "TypeScript at the moment at least doesn't understand this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "And even though this here is a strange error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 111.8,
          "en": "because the plus operator of course would work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.8,
          "end": 113.36,
          "en": "for both numbers and strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.36,
          "end": 117.18,
          "en": "it is also often the case that you accept multiple types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.18,
          "end": 119.66,
          "en": "but you wanna run slightly different code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.66,
          "end": 121.69,
          "en": "depending on the type of data you get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.69,
          "end": 124.77,
          "en": "So that's actually great that we can do this here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 127.75,
          "en": "And we can do this with a traditional if check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.75,
          "end": 131.46,
          "en": "We can check if the typeof num1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.46,
          "end": 133.27,
          "en": "is equal to number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.27,
          "end": 135.7,
          "en": "and this is regular JavaScript code now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.7,
          "end": 137.627,
          "en": "This is not TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.627,
          "end": 140.74,
          "en": "The typeof operator exists in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.74,
          "end": 145.27,
          "en": "and it gives us back the types as strings, number and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.27,
          "end": 147.5,
          "en": "So we can check if num1 is a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.03,
          "end": 151.483,
          "en": "and if num2 is a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.066,
          "end": 156.94299999999998,
          "en": "and if it is we return num1 plus num2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.94,
          "end": 160.85,
          "en": "else if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.763,
          "end": 165.49,
          "en": "typeof num1,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.49,
          "end": 167.84,
          "en": "is let's say a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.05,
          "end": 174.05,
          "en": "and typeof num2 is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.1,
          "end": 178.57,
          "en": "then let's say we wanna return num1 plus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.57,
          "end": 180.57,
          "en": "and then maybe some white space in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 182.09,
          "en": "you don't have to add it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.09,
          "end": 184.29,
          "en": "I'm just doing it here so that we see a difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.29,
          "end": 186.273,
          "en": "besides the different result, I guess.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.55,
          "end": 191.52,
          "en": "Well, and else, if we have mixed types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.52,
          "end": 194.02,
          "en": "it theoretically would work, but in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.02,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "we maybe just want to force a conversion to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 199.38,
          "en": "so that if we get a string and a number mixed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.38,
          "end": 201.57999999999998,
          "en": "we always convert both to a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.57999999999998,
          "end": 203.96,
          "en": "If we have two numbers, we add them like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.96,
          "end": 206.53,
          "en": "If we have two strings, we add them like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.53,
          "end": 208.52,
          "en": "This is a so called Type Guard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.52,
          "end": 210.13,
          "en": "because we run different code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.13,
          "end": 214.19299999999998,
          "en": "based on different types we're getting for our values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.65,
          "end": 217.16,
          "en": "And now you'll see that down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.16,
          "end": 219.85,
          "en": "I'm not able to call this for Booleans",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.85,
          "end": 222.2,
          "en": "because this is neither a number or a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.2,
          "end": 225.03,
          "en": "and I'm only allowing these two kinds of types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.03,
          "end": 228.51,
          "en": "with my Union Type here, hence, we have to remove this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228.51,
          "end": 230.69,
          "en": "And then we can compile this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.69,
          "end": 232.4,
          "en": "It compiles without errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.4,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "And in the generated JavaScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 236.71,
          "en": "of course, the Union Type is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.71,
          "end": 238.67000000000002,
          "en": "The if checks are still there though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.67000000000002,
          "end": 241.89,
          "en": "because as I mentioned that is regular JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.89,
          "end": 245.09,
          "en": "And of course, we don't want that code to magically go away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.09,
          "end": 248.3,
          "en": "In the end it does yield different results.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.3,
          "end": 253.113,
          "en": "So if we now return here and I enter five and 11,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.97,
          "end": 258.18,
          "en": "you see we get both 16 as well as our concatenated string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 261.39300000000003,
          "en": "So Union Types are another key feature.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
